  ["Helm", "helm.svg", "https://helm.sh/docs/", "Packages each app and each add-on as a chart, with values per environment.", "Argo CD, JFrog"],
  ["Jenkins", "jenkins.svg", "https://www.jenkins.io/doc/book/pipeline/", "CI: tests, builds, scans, signs and pushes images, publishes charts, bumps the tag in the gitops repo.", "Azure DevOps, Podman, JFrog"],
  ["JFrog", "jfrog.svg", "https://jfrog.com/help/r/jfrog-artifactory-documentation/helm-chart-repositories", "Artifactory hosts the Helm charts and proxies npm, PyPI and Maven; Curation blocks risky packages, Xray scans what is stored.", "Jenkins, Argo CD, Datadog"],
  ["Kubernetes", "kubernetes.svg", "https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/overview/", "Runs the apps, the website and the add-ons, on EKS and AKS.", "Argo CD, the registries"],
  ["Kyverno", "kyverno.svg", "https://kyverno.io/docs/policy-types/cluster-policy/verify-images/sigstore/", "Admission policies in every cluster: only signed images from our registries may run.", "Kubernetes, Cosign"],
  ["OpenTelemetry", "opentelemetry.svg", "https://opentelemetry.io/docs/collector/", "One protocol, OTLP, and one Collector per cluster for traces, metrics and logs.", "apps, Envoy, S3, Datadog"],
  ["OpenVPN", "openvpn.svg", "https://openvpn.net/community/", "VPN from engineers' laptops to the private subnets that hold the internal UIs.", "laptops, VMs"],
  ["Podman", "podman.svg", "https://docs.podman.io/en/latest/", "Builds images on the Jenkins agents, rootless and without a daemon.", "Jenkins, ECR, ACR"],
  ["Prometheus", "prometheus.svg", "https://prometheus.io/docs/introduction/overview/", "Stores cluster metrics and evaluates alert rules; Alertmanager pages on-call.", "the Collector"],
  ["Secret stores", "keyvault.svg", "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/key-vault/general/overview", "AWS Secrets Manager and Azure Key Vault hold passwords, API keys and the signing keys.", "External Secrets, Cosign"],
  ["Splunk", "splunk.svg", "https://splunk.github.io/splunk-add-on-for-amazon-web-services/SQS-basedS3/", "SIEM: indexes the S3 archive and correlates it with EDR and Wiz findings.", "S3, EDR, Wiz"],
  ["syslog", "syslog.svg", "https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc5424", "The standard log protocol of VMs and network appliances such as the VPN server.", "the Collector"],
  ["Teleport", "teleport.svg", "https://goteleport.com/docs/reference/architecture/agents/", "The one way into production: SSO, short-lived certificates, kubectl and ssh, recorded sessions.", "clusters, VMs, engineers"],
  ["Terraform", "terraform.svg", "https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/backend/s3", "Declares the resources in both clouds; keeps state in S3 or Blob Storage.", "AWS, Azure"],
  ["Trivy", "trivy.svg", "https://trivy.dev/latest/docs/supply-chain/sbom/", "Scans each image for known vulnerabilities in Jenkins and writes its SBOM.", "Jenkins, Cosign"],
  ["Vagrant", "vagrant.svg", "https://developer.hashicorp.com/vagrant/docs/provisioning/ansible", "Local VMs to test Ansible roles before they reach the cloud.", "Ansible"],
  ["Wiz", "wiz.png", "https://www.wiz.io/academy/agentless-scanning", "Agentless cloud security: scans both clouds for misconfigurations and vulnerabilities.", "AWS, Azure, Splunk"],
];
---

<BaseLayout title="Cloud Backend" toc>
  <p class="mono-eyebrow mb-1"><span class="text-accent-blue">$</span> kubectl get all -A</p>
  <h1 class="glitch is-intro mb-4 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-brand-text" data-text="Cloud Backend">Cloud Backend</h1>

  <!-- What is it? -->
  <div class="mb-10 rounded-xl bg-accent-green/15 p-5 sm:p-6">
    <h2 class="mb-1 text-sm font-bold text-brand-text">What is it?</h2>
    <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-brand-body">
      One example backend where common cloud, DevOps and security tools each have a single job: code reaches two clouds
      through Git only, infrastructure changes go through reviewed pull requests, the website sits behind Cloudflare,
      every log lands in one S3 archive, people sign in once and reach production through audited doors, no cloud
      access key lives longer than a few hours, and clusters run only images that CI signed.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- ====== OVERVIEW ====== -->
  <section class="mb-14">
    <p class="mono-eyebrow mb-2">// git push --&gt; production</p>
    <h2 class="glitch mb-4 text-xl font-semibold text-brand-text" data-text="The architecture">The architecture</h2>
    <p class="mb-6 text-brand-body">
      Five flows share the platform: shipping an app, changing the infrastructure, serving the website, collecting logs
      and detecting threats, and operating it. The diagrams after this one zoom in on traffic, logs, identity and
      secrets, and the supply chain; the page ends with the Kubernetes vocabulary.
    </p>

    <figure class="mb-8 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-brand-border bg-white p-4 sm:p-6">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 1000 1375" class="cloud-svg mx-auto block h-auto w-full max-w-[980px] min-w-[860px]" role="img" aria-labelledby="ov-title ov-desc">
        <title id="ov-title">Overview of the example cloud backend across AWS and Azure</title>
        <desc id="ov-desc">At the top, an engineer's laptop with Docker, Vagrant and an EDR agent, and Azure DevOps with the infra, app and gitops repos and Boards. Below, Ansible, Atlantis with Terraform, Jenkins with Podman, JFrog Artifactory and Argo CD with Helm, and Entra ID for every login. Visitors reach Cloudflare, which forwards to Envoy Gateway in the website's EKS cluster. In AWS and Azure: VMs, the ECR and ACR registries, the secret stores and signing keys, the app clusters, the website cluster, and add-ons in every cluster: Prometheus, the Datadog Agent, the OpenTelemetry Collector, the EDR sensor, the Teleport agent, Kyverno and the External Secrets Operator. The Collector and the VMs' syslog feed an S3 log archive, read by Splunk and by Datadog. Wiz scans both clouds, the EDR console receives sensor telemetry, and both report to Splunk. Datadog pages the on-call engineer, who reaches internal tools through OpenVPN and production through Teleport.</desc>
        <defs>
          <marker id="ov" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
            <path d="M1.5 1L8.5 5L1.5 9" fill="none" stroke="context-stroke" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          </marker>
        </defs>

        <!-- frames -->
        <rect class="os-world" x="20" y="40" width="260" height="160" rx="12"/>
        <text class="frame-title" x="32" y="57">Engineer's laptop</text>
        <g>
          <rect x="90" y="161" width="124" height="22" rx="11" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="1.2"/>
          <image href="/logos/edr.svg" x="104" y="165" width="14" height="14"/>
          <text x="122" y="172" dominant-baseline="central" class="pill" fill="#334155">EDR agent</text>
        </g>
        <rect class="os-world" x="340" y="40" width="640" height="120" rx="12"/>
        <image href="/logos/azuredevops.svg" x="353" y="48" width="18" height="18"/>
        <image href="/logos/github.svg" x="375" y="48" width="18" height="18"/>
        <text class="frame-title" x="399" y="57">Azure DevOps: Repos and Boards / GitHub</text>
        <rect class="os-world" x="20" y="560" width="960" height="480" rx="12"/>
        <image href="/logos/amazonwebservices.svg" x="34" y="571" width="30" height="22"/>
        <image href="/logos/azure.svg" x="70" y="573" width="18" height="18"/>
        <text class="frame-title" x="96" y="582">AWS and Azure</text>
        <rect x="280" y="700" width="320" height="150" rx="12" fill="#f7fbf2" stroke="#3b6d11" stroke-width="1.2"/>
        <image href="/logos/kubernetes.svg" x="294" y="711" width="18" height="18"/>
        <text class="frame-title" x="318" y="720" style="fill:#27500a">EKS / AKS: apps</text>
        <rect x="620" y="700" width="350" height="150" rx="12" fill="#f7fbf2" stroke="#3b6d11" stroke-width="1.2"/>
        <image href="/logos/kubernetes.svg" x="634" y="711" width="18" height="18"/>
        <text class="frame-title" x="658" y="720" style="fill:#27500a">EKS: website (AWS)</text>
        <rect x="280" y="865" width="690" height="70" rx="10" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="6 4"/>
        <text class="frame-title" x="292" y="900">In every cluster:</text>
        {addons.map(([label, logo, x, y]) => <CloudPill x={x} y={y} label={label} logo={logo} w={Math.max(110, Math.round(32 + label.length * 6))} />)}

        {ovBoxes.map((b) => <CloudBox {...b} />)}
        {ovArrows.map((a) => <CloudArrow {...a} marker="ov" />)}

        <!-- legend -->
        {ovLegend.map(([color, label, dashed], i) => (
          <g>
            <line x1={ovLegendX[i]} y1="1360" x2={ovLegendX[i] + 34} y2="1360" stroke={color} stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray={dashed ? "5 3" : undefined} marker-end="url(#ov)"/>
            <text class="ts" x={ovLegendX[i] + 44} y="1360" dominant-baseline="central" fill="#475569" style="font-size:11px">{label}</text>
          </g>
        ))}
      </svg>
      <figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm text-brand-muted">
        The cloud box is drawn once: AWS and Azure each run the same pieces, named AWS / Azure; the website cluster and
        the log archive live in AWS only. Argo CD, Atlantis and Jenkins are drawn apart from the clusters but often run
        inside one.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    {stepGroups.map((g) => (
      <>
        <h3 class="mb-4 mt-8 text-lg font-semibold text-brand-text">{g.title}</h3>
        <ol class="space-y-3">
          {g.steps.map((s) => (
            <li class="flex gap-3">
              <span class="mt-0.5 inline-flex h-6 w-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full font-mono text-xs font-semibold text-white" style={`background:${s.color}`}>{s.n}</span>
              <p class="leading-relaxed text-brand-body"><strong class="text-brand-text">{s.title}.</strong> {s.body}</p>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ol>
      </>
    ))}
  </section>

  <!-- ====== TRAFFIC AND ACCESS ====== -->
  <section class="mb-14">
    <p class="mono-eyebrow mb-2">// who gets in, and how</p>
    <h2 class="glitch mb-4 text-xl font-semibold text-brand-text" data-text="Traffic and access">Traffic and access</h2>
    <p class="mb-6 text-brand-body">
      Three doors, one per audience. Visitors only ever reach Cloudflare; engineers use OpenVPN for internal tools and
      Teleport for production, so nothing else listens on the internet.
    </p>

    <figure class="mb-8 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-brand-border bg-white p-4 sm:p-6">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 1000 380" class="cloud-svg mx-auto block h-auto w-full max-w-[980px] min-w-[860px]" role="img" aria-labelledby="ta-title ta-desc">
        <title id="ta-title">Three ways in: the public website, internal tools and production</title>
        <desc id="ta-desc">Public: visitors reach Cloudflare, which forwards through an AWS network load balancer to Envoy Gateway, which routes to the website pods. Internal tools: an engineer's laptop opens an OpenVPN tunnel to the OpenVPN server in the cloud network, which reaches the internal UIs of Jenkins, Argo CD and Atlantis. Production: the engineer logs in to the Teleport proxy, which reaches Teleport agents over reverse tunnels, which give kubectl access to the clusters and ssh access to the VMs.</desc>
        <defs>
          <marker id="ta" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
            <path d="M1.5 1L8.5 5L1.5 9" fill="none" stroke="context-stroke" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          </marker>
        </defs>
        {taLanes.map((lane) => (
          <g>
            <text class="th" x="16" y={lane.y + 32} dominant-baseline="central" fill="#1e293b">{lane.name}</text>
            <text class="ts" x="16" y={lane.y + 50} dominant-baseline="central" fill="#64748b">{lane.sub}</text>
            {lane.boxes.map((b, i) => <CloudBox {...b} x={taX(i)} y={lane.y} w={190} h={80} />)}
            {lane.boxes.slice(1).map((_, i) => (
              <CloudArrow d={`M${taX(i) + 191} ${lane.y + 40} L${taX(i + 1) - 2} ${lane.y + 40}`} color={lane.color} marker="ta" />
            ))}
          </g>
        ))}
      </svg>
      <figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm text-brand-muted">
        Sources:{" "}
        <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/ssl/origin-configuration/authenticated-origin-pull/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>authenticated origin pulls</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/network/introduction.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>AWS NLB</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://gateway.envoyproxy.io/docs/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>Envoy Gateway</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://openvpn.net/community/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>OpenVPN</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/clientvpn-admin/what-is.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>AWS Client VPN (OpenVPN-based)</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://goteleport.com/docs/reference/architecture/agents/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>Teleport agents</a>.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <!-- ====== LOGS ====== -->
  <section class="mb-14">
    <p class="mono-eyebrow mb-2">// everything lands in S3</p>
    <h2 class="glitch mb-4 text-xl font-semibold text-brand-text" data-text="Logs, metrics and security">Logs, metrics and security</h2>
    <p class="mb-6 text-brand-body">
      Logs go to one S3 archive first, and the monitoring tools read from it, so no tool owns the only copy and a new tool
      can replay history. Metrics and traces go straight to the tools that graph them, and security findings to the SIEM.
    </p>

    <figure class="mb-8 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-brand-border bg-white p-4 sm:p-6">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 1000 580" class="cloud-svg mx-auto block h-auto w-full max-w-[980px] min-w-[860px]" role="img" aria-labelledby="lg-title lg-desc">
        <title id="lg-title">Where logs, metrics and security findings go</title>
        <desc id="lg-desc">Four columns: sources, collect, store and use. Argo CD and JFrog report to Datadog through its integrations. Apps and Envoy send OTLP, and VMs and the OpenVPN server send syslog, to the OpenTelemetry Collector, which sends metrics to Prometheus, traces and metrics to Datadog, and logs to the S3 log archive. Cloudflare writes to S3 with Logpush, and AWS writes CloudTrail and VPC flow logs there. Datadog and Splunk both read the archive. EDR sensors on laptops, VMs and nodes report to the EDR console, and Wiz scans the cloud accounts; both send their findings to Splunk.</desc>
        <defs>
          <marker id="lg" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
            <path d="M1.5 1L8.5 5L1.5 9" fill="none" stroke="context-stroke" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          </marker>
        </defs>
        <text class="divider-label" x="120" y="28" text-anchor="middle">SOURCES</text>
        <text class="divider-label" x="350" y="28" text-anchor="middle">COLLECT</text>
        <text class="divider-label" x="560" y="28" text-anchor="middle">STORE</text>
        <text class="divider-label" x="835" y="28" text-anchor="middle">USE</text>

        {lgBoxes.map((b) => <CloudBox {...b} />)}
        {lgArrows.map((a) => <CloudArrow {...a} marker="lg" />)}

        <line x1="20" y1="560" x2="54" y2="560" stroke={flow.logs} stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#lg)"/>
        <text class="ts" x="64" y="560" dominant-baseline="central" fill="#475569" style="font-size:11px">logs</text>
        <line x1="160" y1="560" x2="194" y2="560" stroke={flow.metrics} stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#lg)"/>
        <text class="ts" x="204" y="560" dominant-baseline="central" fill="#475569" style="font-size:11px">metrics and traces</text>
        <line x1="360" y1="560" x2="394" y2="560" stroke={flow.security} stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#lg)"/>
        <text class="ts" x="404" y="560" dominant-baseline="central" fill="#475569" style="font-size:11px">security events and findings</text>
      </svg>
      <figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm text-brand-muted">
        Azure's logs reach the same archive through the Collector. Sources:{" "}
        <a href="https://opentelemetry.io/docs/specs/otlp/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>OTLP</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector-contrib/tree/main/receiver/syslogreceiver" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>syslog receiver</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector-contrib/tree/main/exporter/awss3exporter" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>S3 exporter</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector-contrib/tree/main/exporter/datadogexporter" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>Datadog exporter</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://www.envoyproxy.io/docs/envoy/latest/api-v3/config/trace/v3/opentelemetry.proto" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>Envoy OpenTelemetry tracer</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/logs/logpush/logpush-job/enable-destinations/aws-s3/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>Logpush to S3</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/cloudtrail-user-guide.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>CloudTrail</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/object-lock.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>S3 Object Lock</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/object-lifecycle-mgmt.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>S3 lifecycle</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://splunk.github.io/splunk-add-on-for-amazon-web-services/SQS-basedS3/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>Splunk SQS-based S3 input</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://docs.datadoghq.com/logs/guide/forwarder/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>Datadog Forwarder</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://docs.datadoghq.com/integrations/argocd/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>Datadog for Argo CD</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://docs.datadoghq.com/integrations/jfrog-platform-cloud/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>Datadog for JFrog Cloud</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://www.wiz.io/academy/agentless-scanning" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>agentless scanning</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://splunkbase.splunk.com/app/6676" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>Wiz Add-on for Splunk</a>.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <!-- ====== IDENTITY AND SECRETS ====== -->
  <section class="mb-14">
    <p class="mono-eyebrow mb-2">// no long-lived keys</p>
    <h2 class="glitch mb-4 text-xl font-semibold text-brand-text" data-text="Identity and secrets">Identity and secrets</h2>
    <p class="mb-6 text-brand-body">
      People sign in once, through Entra ID, and machines never use a stored cloud key: every credential is issued on demand
      and expires within hours, so a copied file or a leaked log line stops working by itself. Leaving someone's Entra
      group removes their access everywhere within hours.
    </p>

    <figure class="mb-8 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-brand-border bg-white p-4 sm:p-6">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 1000 420" class="cloud-svg mx-auto block h-auto w-full max-w-[980px] min-w-[860px]" role="img" aria-labelledby="id-title id-desc">
        <title id="id-title">How people, pods and pipelines get credentials</title>
        <desc id="id-desc">People: an engineer signs in to Entra ID with MFA, which hands out short-lived access through IAM Identity Center, az login and Teleport certificates to the clouds and clusters; Azure DevOps, Argo CD, Jenkins, JFrog, Datadog, Splunk and Wiz use the same Entra ID login. Workloads: the External Secrets Operator reads Secrets Manager and Key Vault with EKS Pod Identity or AKS Workload ID and writes Kubernetes Secrets that the app pods read. Pipelines: Jenkins and Atlantis run on VMs whose instance profile or managed identity yields short-lived tokens for the cloud APIs.</desc>
        <defs>
          <marker id="id" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
            <path d="M1.5 1L8.5 5L1.5 9" fill="none" stroke="context-stroke" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          </marker>
        </defs>
        {idLanes.map((lane) => (
          <g>
            <text class="th" x="16" y={lane.y + 32} dominant-baseline="central" fill="#1e293b">{lane.name}</text>
            <text class="ts" x="16" y={lane.y + 50} dominant-baseline="central" fill="#64748b">{lane.sub}</text>
            {lane.boxes.map((b, i) => <CloudBox {...b} x={taX(i)} y={lane.y} w={190} h={80} />)}
            {lane.boxes.slice(1).map((_, i) => (
              <CloudArrow d={`M${taX(i) + 191} ${lane.y + 40} L${taX(i + 1) - 2} ${lane.y + 40}`} color={lane.color} marker="id" />
            ))}
          </g>
        ))}
        <CloudArrow d={`M${taX(1) + 95} 121 L${taX(1) + 95} 138`} color={flow.ops} marker="id" />
        <rect x="150" y="140" width="840" height="34" rx="10" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="6 4"/>
        <text class="frame-title" x="162" y="157">Same Entra ID login:</text>
        {ssoTools.map(([label, logo], i) => <CloudPill x={ssoX[i]} y={147} w={ssoW[i]} label={label} logo={logo} color={flow.ops} />)}
      </svg>
      <figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm text-brand-muted">
        Teleport needs its Enterprise edition to sign in through Entra ID; the Community Edition only offers GitHub.
        Pods that call cloud APIs themselves, such as an app writing to S3, use the same pod identity without going
        through a Secret. Sources:{" "}
        <a href="https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/idp-microsoft-entra.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>Entra ID with IAM Identity Center</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://goteleport.com/docs/zero-trust-access/sso/azuread/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>Teleport with Entra ID</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://argo-cd.readthedocs.io/en/stable/operator-manual/user-management/microsoft/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>Argo CD with Entra ID</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://plugins.jenkins.io/azure-ad/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>Jenkins Entra ID plugin</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://external-secrets.io/latest/provider/aws-secrets-manager/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>External Secrets for AWS</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://external-secrets.io/latest/provider/azure-key-vault/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>and for Key Vault</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/pod-identities.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>EKS Pod Identity</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/aks/workload-identity-overview" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>AKS Workload ID</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_use_switch-role-ec2.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>EC2 instance roles</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/managed-identities-azure-resources/overview" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>Azure managed identities</a>.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <!-- ====== SUPPLY CHAIN ====== -->
  <section class="mb-14">
    <p class="mono-eyebrow mb-2">// only signed images run</p>
    <h2 class="glitch mb-4 text-xl font-semibold text-brand-text" data-text="Supply chain">Supply chain</h2>
    <p class="mb-6 text-brand-body">
      Every change passes a row of gates, and any gate can stop it: a secret never lands in Git, a risky package never
      enters the cache, and a cluster runs only images that CI signed. Infrastructure has its own gates, and Wiz checks
      afterwards for what got through or was changed by hand.
    </p>

    <figure class="mb-8 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-brand-border bg-white p-4 sm:p-6">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 1000 274" class="cloud-svg mx-auto block h-auto w-full max-w-[980px] min-w-[860px]" role="img" aria-labelledby="sc-title sc-desc">
        <title id="sc-title">Gates between a commit and production</title>
        <desc id="sc-desc">Apps: push protection in Azure Repos rejects secrets, JFrog Curation blocks risky packages, Trivy scans the image and writes its SBOM, Cosign signs image and SBOM with a KMS key, and Kyverno admits only images signed by that key. Infrastructure: an infra pull request, Atlantis runs terraform plan, Conftest checks the plan against Rego rules, Terraform applies after review, and Wiz finds what slipped by or was changed by hand.</desc>
        <defs>
          <marker id="sc" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
            <path d="M1.5 1L8.5 5L1.5 9" fill="none" stroke="context-stroke" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          </marker>
        </defs>
        {scLanes.map((lane) => (
          <g>
            <text class="th" x="16" y={lane.y + 34} dominant-baseline="central" fill="#1e293b">{lane.name}</text>
            <text class="ts" x="16" y={lane.y + 52} dominant-baseline="central" fill="#64748b">{lane.sub}</text>
            {lane.boxes.map((b, i) => <CloudBox {...b} x={scX(i)} y={lane.y} w={152} h={84} />)}
            {lane.boxes.slice(1).map((_, i) => (
              <CloudArrow d={`M${scX(i) + 153} ${lane.y + 42} L${scX(i + 1) - 2} ${lane.y + 42}`} color={lane.color} marker="sc" />
            ))}
          </g>
        ))}
      </svg>
      <figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm text-brand-muted">
        Xray still scans what Artifactory stores, Helm charts included; its download blocking for remote repositories
        moves to Curation during 2026. Sources:{" "}
        <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/repos/security/github-advanced-security-secret-scanning?view=azure-devops" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>push protection in Azure Repos</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://docs.jfrog.com/security/docs/curation-intro" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>JFrog Curation</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://docs.jfrog.com/security/docs/create-policies" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>Xray policies</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://trivy.dev/latest/docs/supply-chain/sbom/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>Trivy SBOM</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://docs.sigstore.dev/cosign/key_management/overview/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>Cosign with KMS</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://docs.sigstore.dev/cosign/verifying/attestation/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>SBOM attestations</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://kyverno.io/docs/policy-types/cluster-policy/verify-images/sigstore/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>Kyverno image verification</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://www.runatlantis.io/docs/policy-checking.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>Atlantis policy checks</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://www.conftest.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>Conftest</a>.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <!-- ====== TOOLS ====== -->
  <section class="mb-14">
    <p class="mono-eyebrow mb-2">// one job each</p>
    <h2 class="glitch mb-4 text-xl font-semibold text-brand-text" data-text="Who does what">Who does what</h2>
    <div class="mb-4 overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full min-w-[640px] border-collapse text-sm">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-brand-border text-left text-brand-text">
            <th class="w-[18%] py-2 pr-4 font-semibold">Tool</th>
            <th class="w-[54%] py-2 pr-4 font-semibold">Job in this model</th>
            <th class="w-[28%] py-2 font-semibold">Talks to</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="align-top text-brand-body">
          {tools.map(([name, logo, url, job, peers], i) => (
            <tr class={i < tools.length - 1 ? "border-b border-brand-border/60" : ""}>
              <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium"><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 whitespace-nowrap"><img src={`/logos/${logo}`} alt="" width="18" height="18" class="h-[18px] w-[18px] shrink-0 rounded-sm bg-white object-contain p-px" loading="lazy"/><a href={url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>{name}</a></span></td>
              <td class="py-2 pr-4">{job}</td>
              <td class="py-2 text-brand-muted">{peers}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <p class="rounded-lg border border-brand-border bg-brand-bg px-4 py-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-brand-muted">
      <strong class="text-brand-text">Other choices.</strong> This is one coherent model, not the only one. The
      comparisons below cover the Git host, CI, monitoring and VPN. Docker and Podman build the same OCI images, so the
      laptop and CI can differ. EDR is a category:
      CrowdStrike Falcon, Microsoft Defender for Endpoint and SentinelOne all fit that box. HashiCorp Vault could
      replace both cloud secret stores with one, and issue database passwords on demand. gitleaks in a pre-commit hook
      catches a secret before it even leaves the laptop. OPA Gatekeeper can replace Kyverno, Checkov can replace
      Conftest, and Grype and Syft can replace Trivy. Sources:{" "}
      <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/service-hooks/services/jenkins" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>Azure DevOps to Jenkins</a>,{" "}
      <a href="https://www.runatlantis.io/docs/access-credentials.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>Atlantis Git hosts</a>,{" "}
      <a href="https://argo-cd.readthedocs.io/en/stable/operator-manual/declarative-setup/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>Argo CD clusters</a>,{" "}
      <a href="https://jfrog.com/help/r/jfrog-artifactory-documentation/remote-repositories" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>Artifactory remote repositories</a>,{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/prometheus-community/helm-charts/tree/main/charts/kube-prometheus-stack" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>kube-prometheus-stack</a>,{" "}
      <a href="https://prometheus.io/docs/alerting/latest/alertmanager/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>Alertmanager</a>,{" "}
      <a href="https://goteleport.com/docs/reference/helm-reference/teleport-kube-agent/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>teleport-kube-agent</a>,{" "}
      <a href="https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/backend/azurerm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>azurerm backend</a>,{" "}
      <a href="https://docs.ansible.com/ansible/latest/collections/azure/azcollection/azure_rm_inventory.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>Azure inventory</a>,{" "}
      <a href="https://developer.hashicorp.com/vault/docs/secrets/databases" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>Vault database secrets</a>,{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/gitleaks/gitleaks" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>gitleaks</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- ====== COMPARISONS ====== -->
  <section class="mb-14">
    <p class="mono-eyebrow mb-2">// pick one per row</p>
    <h2 class="glitch mb-4 text-xl font-semibold text-brand-text" data-text="Interchangeable pieces">Interchangeable pieces</h2>
    <p class="mb-6 text-brand-body">
      Four places in the overview carry a slash: either tool fits there, and the rest of the model stays the same.
      The first column is the one the steps above describe; for monitoring they use both.
    </p>

    {comparisons.map((c) => (
      <>
        <h3 class="mb-3 mt-8 text-lg font-semibold text-brand-text">{c.title}</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed text-brand-body">{c.intro}</p>
        <div class="mb-3 overflow-x-auto">
          <table class={`w-full border-collapse text-sm ${c.options.length > 2 ? "min-w-[860px]" : "min-w-[640px]"}`}>
            <thead>
              <tr class="border-b border-brand-border text-left text-brand-text">
                <th class="w-[16%] py-2 pr-4 font-semibold"></th>
                {c.options.map((o, i) => (
                  <th class="py-2 pr-4 align-bottom" style={`width:${84 / c.options.length}%`}>
                    <span class={`inline-flex items-center gap-2 ${i === 0 ? "font-bold" : "font-medium"}`}>
                      {(Array.isArray(o.logo) ? o.logo : [o.logo]).map((l) => (
                        <img src={`/logos/${l}`} alt="" width="18" height="18" class="h-[18px] w-[18px] shrink-0 rounded-sm bg-white object-contain p-px" loading="lazy"/>
                      ))}
                      {o.name}
                    </span>
                  </th>
                ))}
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="align-top text-brand-body">
              {c.rows.map(([criterion, ...cells], i) => (
                <tr class={i < c.rows.length - 1 ? "border-b border-brand-border/60" : ""}>
                  <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium text-brand-text">{criterion}</td>
                  {cells.map((cell) => <td class="py-2 pr-4">{cell}</td>)}
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        {c.note && <p class="mb-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-brand-muted">{c.note}</p>}
        <p class="text-sm text-brand-muted">
          Sources:{" "}
          {c.sources.map(([label, url], i) => (
            <>
              <a href={url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>{label}</a>{i < c.sources.length - 1 ? ", " : "."}
            </>
          ))}
        </p>
      </>
    ))}
  </section>

  <!-- ====== KUBERNETES VOCABULARY ====== -->
  <section class="mb-14">
    <p class="mono-eyebrow mb-2">// kubectl api-resources</p>
    <h2 class="glitch mb-4 text-xl font-semibold text-brand-text" data-text="Kubernetes vocabulary">Kubernetes vocabulary</h2>
    <p class="mb-6 text-brand-body">
      A cluster has two halves: the control plane, which stores what you asked for and decides where it runs, and the
      nodes, which run it. On EKS and AKS the cloud runs the control plane; you get its API and bring the nodes, unless you pick EKS Auto Mode or AKS Automatic, where the cloud manages them too. The
      first diagram shows the parts of a cluster, the second the objects you write into it, and the table defines each
      word.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mb-4 mt-8 text-lg font-semibold text-brand-text">The parts of a cluster</h3>
    <figure class="mb-8 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-brand-border bg-white p-4 sm:p-6">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 1000 660" class="cloud-svg mx-auto block h-auto w-full max-w-[980px] min-w-[860px]" role="img" aria-labelledby="k8-title k8-desc">
        <title id="k8-title">The components of a Kubernetes cluster</title>
        <desc id="k8-desc">Clients such as kubectl and Argo CD call the kube-apiserver. In the control plane, run by EKS or AKS, the API server is the only component that talks to etcd, and the kube-scheduler, the kube-controller-manager and the cloud-controller-manager all watch and update the API server. Below, two nodes, each a VM, run a kubelet that watches the API server for its pods, the containerd runtime and kube-proxy; the CNI plugin gives each pod an IP. Each node runs a web pod from a Deployment and an agent pod from a DaemonSet.</desc>
        <defs>
          <marker id="k8" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
            <path d="M1.5 1L8.5 5L1.5 9" fill="none" stroke="context-stroke" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          </marker>
        </defs>

        <rect class="os-world" x="20" y="105" width="960" height="235" rx="12"/>
        <image href="/logos/kubernetes.svg" x="32" y="113" width="18" height="18"/>
        <text class="frame-title" x="56" y="122">Control plane (EKS / AKS run it)</text>

        {k8sNodes.map((node) => (
          <g>
            <rect class="os-world" x={node.ox} y="390" width="470" height="250" rx="12"/>
            <text class="frame-title" x={node.ox + 12} y="407">{node.name}</text>
            <CloudPill x={node.ox + 458 - cniW} y={397} w={cniW} label={cniLabel} color="#3b6d11" />
            {k8sNodeBoxes(node.ox).map((b) => <CloudBox {...b} />)}
            <CloudArrow d={`M${node.ox + 156} 460 L${node.ox + 163} 460`} color={k8sArrow} marker="k8" />
            {node.pods.map(([title, container, ip], i) => {
              const px = node.ox + 15 + i * 225;
              return (
                <g>
                  <rect x={px} y="515" width="215" height="105" rx="10" fill="#f7fbf2" stroke="#3b6d11" stroke-width="1.2"/>
                  <text class="frame-title" x={px + 12} y="532" style="fill:#27500a">{title}</text>
                  <CloudPill x={px + 12} y={547} label={container} color={flow.app} />
                  <CloudPill x={px + 12} y={577} label={ip} />
                </g>
              );
            })}
          </g>
        ))}

        {k8sControl.map((b) => <CloudBox {...b} />)}
        <CloudArrow d="M370 92 L370 138" color={k8sArrow} marker="k8" label={[382, 113, "HTTPS", "start"]} />
        <path d="M214 230 L246 230" stroke={k8sArrow} stroke-width="2" fill="none" marker-start="url(#k8)" marker-end="url(#k8)"/>
        <CloudArrow d="M538 168 L492 168" color={k8sArrow} marker="k8" />
        <CloudArrow d="M538 230 L492 230" color={k8sArrow} marker="k8" />
        <CloudArrow d="M538 292 L492 292" color={k8sArrow} marker="k8" />
        <CloudArrow d="M140 423 L140 360 L300 360 L300 322" color={k8sArrow} marker="k8" />
        <CloudArrow d="M630 423 L630 360 L440 360 L440 322" color={k8sArrow} marker="k8" label={[370, 373, "kubelets watch the API for their pods", "middle"]} />
      </svg>
      <figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm text-brand-muted">
        Arrows point to whoever is called. The controllers and the kubelets never call each other: they watch the API
        for changes and write their results back. Only the API server talks to etcd; it also calls the kubelet for
        kubectl logs and exec. Sources:{" "}
        <a href="https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/overview/components/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>cluster components</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/eks-architecture.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>EKS architecture</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/aks/core-aks-concepts" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>AKS core concepts</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://kubernetes.io/docs/reference/networking/virtual-ips/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>kube-proxy modes</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://github.com/aws/amazon-vpc-cni-k8s" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>Amazon VPC CNI</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/aks/concepts-network-cni-overview" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>Azure CNI</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://kubernetes.io/docs/reference/access-authn-authz/extensible-admission-controllers/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>admission webhooks</a>.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <h3 class="mb-4 mt-8 text-lg font-semibold text-brand-text">The objects you write</h3>
    <figure class="mb-8 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-brand-border bg-white p-4 sm:p-6">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 1000 445" class="cloud-svg mx-auto block h-auto w-full max-w-[980px] min-w-[860px]" role="img" aria-labelledby="ko-title ko-desc">
        <title id="ko-title">The Kubernetes objects behind one app</title>
        <desc id="ko-desc">In the namespace web: a HorizontalPodAutoscaler sets the replicas of a Deployment, which creates a ReplicaSet, which creates the pods. A Gateway's listener passes requests to an HTTPRoute, which picks a Service, which selects the pods by label. Each pod uses a ConfigMap, a Secret, a ServiceAccount and a PersistentVolumeClaim. Outside any namespace: Node, Namespace, PersistentVolume, StorageClass, GatewayClass, ClusterRole and CustomResourceDefinition.</desc>
        <defs>
          <marker id="ko" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
            <path d="M1.5 1L8.5 5L1.5 9" fill="none" stroke="context-stroke" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          </marker>
        </defs>

        <rect class="os-world" x="20" y="20" width="960" height="345" rx="12"/>
        <image href="/logos/kubernetes.svg" x="32" y="28" width="18" height="18"/>
        <text class="frame-title" x="56" y="37">Namespace: web</text>

        <rect x="770" y="185" width="200" height="100" rx="10" fill="#eaf3de" stroke="#3b6d11" stroke-width="1.2"/>
        <rect x="765" y="180" width="200" height="100" rx="10" fill="#eaf3de" stroke="#3b6d11" stroke-width="1.2"/>
        {k8sObjects.map((b) => <CloudBox {...b} />)}
        {k8sObjArrows.map((a) => <CloudArrow {...a} marker="ko" />)}

        <rect x="40" y="305" width="920" height="40" rx="10" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="6 4"/>
        <text class="frame-title" x="52" y="325">Used by each pod:</text>
        {podUses.map((p) => <CloudPill x={p.x} y={315} w={p.w} label={p.label} color={flow.app} />)}

        <rect x="20" y="385" width="960" height="40" rx="10" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="6 4"/>
        <text class="frame-title" x="32" y="405">Cluster-wide objects:</text>
        {clusterWide.map((p) => <CloudPill x={p.x} y={395} w={p.w} label={p.label} />)}
      </svg>
      <figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm text-brand-muted">
        Objects find each other by name or by label: the Service and the ReplicaSet both find their pods through the
        label app=web, so a pod with the wrong label gets no traffic. Sources:{" "}
        <a href="https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/workloads/controllers/deployment/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>Deployments</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/workloads/controllers/daemonset/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>DaemonSets</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/services-networking/service/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>Services</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://gateway-api.sigs.k8s.io/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>Gateway API</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/services-networking/ingress/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>Ingress, frozen</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/configuration/secret/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>Secrets</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/storage/persistent-volumes/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>persistent volumes</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/workloads/autoscaling/horizontal-pod-autoscale/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>HorizontalPodAutoscaler</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://kubernetes.io/docs/reference/access-authn-authz/rbac/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>RBAC</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/extend-kubernetes/api-extension/custom-resources/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>custom resources</a>.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <h3 class="mb-4 mt-8 text-lg font-semibold text-brand-text">Glossary</h3>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full min-w-[640px] border-collapse text-sm">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-brand-border text-left text-brand-text">
            <th class="w-[22%] py-2 pr-4 font-semibold">Term</th>
            <th class="w-[46%] py-2 pr-4 font-semibold">What it is</th>
            <th class="w-[32%] py-2 font-semibold">In this model</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="align-top text-brand-body">
          {k8sTerms.map(([term, what, here], i) => (
            <tr class={i < k8sTerms.length - 1 ? "border-b border-brand-border/60" : ""}>
              <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium text-brand-text">{term}</td>
              <td class="py-2 pr-4">{what}</td>
              <td class="py-2 text-brand-muted">{here}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

